---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Container } from "design-system-base";
---

<Layout
  title="Research Methodology — Metabolic 40+"
  description="Our approach to researching and validating health content for adults over 40."
  type="website"
>
  <Container class="py-16 sm:py-20 max-w-3xl">
    <article class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Research Methodology</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Our approach to evidence-based content</p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Evidence Hierarchy</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            We prioritize research in the following order of evidence strength:
          </p>
          <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 space-y-2">
            <li>Systematic reviews and meta-analyses</li>
            <li>RCTs (Randomized Controlled Trials)</li>
            <li>Prospective cohort studies</li>
            <li>Case-control studies</li>
            <li>Expert clinical consensus</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Age-Specific Considerations</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            When researching topics for adults over 40, we specifically look for:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 space-y-2">
            <li>Studies with participants aged 40+ (or clear age-stratified data)</li>
            <li>Research on hormonal changes and metabolic shifts</li>
            <li>Long-term outcome studies rather than short-term interventions</li>
            <li>Safety data for middle-aged and older adults</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Source Verification</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Every claim we make is backed by a primary source. We:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 space-y-2">
            <li>Link directly to peer-reviewed journals when possible</li>
            <li>Verify author credentials and institutional affiliations</li>
            <li>Cross-reference findings across multiple independent studies</li>
            <li>Note limitations and conflicting evidence transparently</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Content Updates</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Medical research evolves rapidly. We review and update our content annually, 
            or sooner when significant new evidence emerges. Updated articles are marked 
            with a revision date.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Container>
</Layout>